Description: pco: test one descriptor field for null instead of every dword
 trans_is_null_desc() compares every dword of a descriptor with zero and
 ANDs the results: 4 dwords for a buffer, 4 for a combined image sampler,
 the whole stride for an image or texel buffer. A null descriptor is all
 zeros (pvr_arch_descriptor_set.c memsets it), and every valid descriptor
 has a field that is never zero: the size of a buffer descriptor (dword 2,
 the bound range, which Vulkan requires to be non-zero; pco reads the size
 there for get_ubo_size as well) and the texture address in image state
 word 1 (dwords 2 and 3; TEXSTATE IMAGE_WORD1 texaddr, all pvr heaps start
 above zero). Test only those. An inline uniform block can never be null.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
